    col
      h2 New look and feel
      text All colors have been carefully and manually redefined for a more contrasted, neutral (less bluish) look and feel.
      text The default color theme is much more accessible. Most colors now follow the WCAG 2.1 AAA standard, and some secondary muted colors follow the WCAG 2.1 AA standard.
      text Focus states have been improved for more consistency and contrast, and spacings have been reduced for a sleeker and more neutral style.
      h2 Easier customization#
      text We have refactored all  files to make it easier for you to compile your version of Pico with . All modules can now be enabled or disabled using .
      text .scss
      link SASS /docs/sass
      link "@use" https://sass-lang.com/documentation/at-rules/use
      text We added more , now totaling over 130, to easily create a unique look and feel, enhancing design flexibility.
      link "CSS variables" /docs/css-variables
      h2 Color palette#
      text Pico v2 comes with  to help you personalize your brand design system. The colors can be imported into any file, and a new stylesheet with all the color utilities is provided.
      link "380 manually crafted colors" /docs/colors
      text .scss
      h2 Better breakpoints#
      text We have updated the  to follow the width of standard devices and added a new breakpoint for larger screens.
      link breakpoints /docs/container
      h2 Group component#
      text With  (), you can now stack forms elements and buttons horizontally.
      row
        link group /docs/group
        text "role=\"group\""
      h2 Conditional Styling#
      text is a powerful feature that allows you to apply styles selectively by wrapping elements in  containers, which is ideal for mixed-style environments. This method restricts styling to designated sections, making it particularly useful for combining multiple stylesheets or components seamlessly.
      link "Conditional Styling" /docs/conditional
      text .pico
      h2 Version picker#
      text Play with the , which offers 20 precompiled color themes accessible via CDN for all Pico versions. The total number of combinations is over 100.
      link "Version Picker" /docs/version-picker
      h2 Breaking changes#
      h3 CSS Vars
      text All  are prefixed with to avoid collisions with other CSS frameworks or your vars. We also added new CSS variables and renamed some to follow a consistent pattern.
      link "CSS custom properties" /docs/css-variables
      text pico-
      text {component}-{state}-{property}
      h3 SCSS files
      text We renamed and moved many .scss files. If you import Pico modules, you need to update your paths.
      h3 Buttons
      text are not  by default anymore. Only form buttons are full-width to be consistent with other form elements.
      row
        link Buttons /docs/button
        text width: 100%;
      h3 Table
      text The  class is now used for the striped ’s style.
      row
        text .striped
        link table /docs/table
      h3 Dropdowns
      text While  are still classless,  now use. We also removed the experimental syntax that allowed dropdowns in the nav using nested lists.
      row
        link accordions /docs/accordion
        link dropdowns /docs/dropdown
        text .dropdown
      h3 Grid
      text columns now collapse on small devices ().
      row
        link Grid /docs/grid
        text <768px
      h3 Figure
      text We removed the  from  and introduced a new utility class,, to enable horizontal scrolling on any element.
      text overflow-x: auto;
      text <figure>
      card
        link .overflow-auto /docs/v2/docs/overflow-auto
